                <span class="mock__chip">capability/not-implemented</span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="works">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>What works today</h2>
                <p>The framework and the contracts exist. The spreadsheet engine does not.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="works__grid">
                <article class="works__col">
                    <h3>Framework</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Workspace build with static profile</li>
                        <li>Command line surface</li>
                        <li>Capability matrix from the host</li>
                        <li>Studio shell, empty on purpose</li>
                        <li>Skills package</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="works__col">
                    <h3>Contracts</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Handle-based workbook API</li>
                        <li>Monotonic revisions</li>
                        <li>Stable error codes</li>
                        <li>Per-format capability matrix</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="works__col works__col--muted">
                    <h3>Not yet</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Workbook parser</li>
                        <li>Formula engine</li>
                        <li>Pivot aggregates</li>
                        <li>XLSX writer</li>
                        <li>Cell renderer</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="pillars">
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">01</span>
                <h2>Workbooks</h2>
                <p>
                    A workbook project keeps stable sheet ids, order-only
                    indexes and monotonic revisions, so a stale writer is
                    rejected instead of silently overwriting.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">02</span>
                <h2>Formula intelligence</h2>
                <p>
                    Six declared checks cover formulas, references, cycles,
                    types, ranges and styles. Every finding carries a sheet id
                    and an A1 address, never a single quality score.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">03</span>
                <h2>Agent authoring</h2>
                <p>
                    An agent receives the workbook, the template and the rules.
                    It maps the sheets, fills formulas, runs inspection and
                    reports what it could not do.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <section class="flow">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>A workbook task, end to end</h2>
                <p>Four steps the product is designed around. Only the contracts are declared.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="flow__list">
                <li class="flow__item">
                    <span class="flow__index">01</span>
                    <h3>Read workbook <span class="chip">planned</span></h3>
                    <p>Open the project or classify an import. Support is read from the matrix, not the suffix.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="flow__item">
                    <span class="flow__index">02</span>
                    <h3>Map sheets <span class="chip">planned</span></h3>
                    <p>Match sheet ids and names to the task, and keep the mapping stable across revisions.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="flow__item">
                    <span class="flow__index">03</span>
                    <h3>Inspect formulas <span class="chip">declared</span></h3>
                    <p>Run the six declared checks and attach every finding to a sheet id and cell address.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="flow__item">
                    <span class="flow__index">04</span>
                    <h3>Export <span class="chip">declared</span></h3>
                    <p>Write a declared target and return a loss report describing what the format kept.</p>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="note">Declared means the contract exists. Planned means the engine does not.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="formats">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Format matrix</h2>
                <p>Ten declared formats. None are importable, editable, exportable or inspectable in this build.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Format</th>
